20 RAG interview questions across 3 difficulty levels — click any question to reveal the answer, filter by level, or hit "Ask Claude to explain deeper" for any topic.

Here's a quick cheat sheet on what each level covers:

**Basic (6 questions)** — definitions, components, chunking, embeddings, vector databases, RAG vs fine-tuning. Expect these in any junior/mid-level role.

**Intermediate (7 questions)** — hybrid search, re-ranking, query transformation, multi-turn conversations, evaluation metrics (RAGAS), context window management, metadata filtering. These show you've actually built a RAG system.

**Advanced (7 questions)** — lost-in-the-middle problem, Agentic RAG, system design at scale, RAPTOR, hallucination prevention, GraphRAG, handling conflicting documents. These separate candidates who've shipped RAG in production.

The most commonly asked questions in real interviews are hybrid search, re-ranking, evaluation metrics, and hallucination prevention — interviewers want to know you understand the failure modes, not just the happy path.